WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.410
- So the US midterm
elections are coming up fast

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.460
and the results can have a huge impact

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.760
on the final two years of
President Donald Trump's

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.080
current term in office

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.380
and if you're wondering what
the hell midterm elections are?

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.213
Don't worry!

00:00:11.216 --> 00:00:14.053
'Cause I'm about to let
you know in 60 seconds,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.753
right after I eat this Carolina Reaper.

00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:22.905
(crunching pepper)

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.783
Oh, my god.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.360
Basically midterm elections take place,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.810
as the name implies, at the halfway point

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.200
between presidential elections

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.917
and federal election during
which members of Congress

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:32.640
are selected by voters.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.042
This includes all 435 members

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:35.742
of the US House of Representatives

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.320
and one third of US Senators.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.470
This year if Democrats
were to win the house

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.810
they'd be able to (gasping)

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.475
They would be able to, oh god!
(banging on wall)

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:45.713
- [Cameraman] 20 seconds.

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:46.880
Finish it off.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.670
- This year, oh I can't do it.
(record scratching to a halt)

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.120
I'm gonna do the full
monologue one time clean.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.800
I need to make sure I get these takes

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.940
because afterwards I won't
be able to do a clean take.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.640
Basically midterm elections take place,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.470
as the name implies, at the halfway point

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.830
between presidential elections

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.980
and our federal elections
during which members of Congress

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.203
are selected by voters.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.430
This includes all 435 members

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.820
of the US House of Representatives

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.753
and one third of US Senators.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.560
You might be wondering,
what's so important?

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.270
Because maybe this is
quite as jazzy sounding

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.230
as presidential elections but no,

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.980
these elections are incredibly important

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.340
because the results will dictate

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.440
whether the Democratic or Republican party

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.065
will control each chamber of Congress

00:01:24.065 --> 00:01:25.920
and whichever party controls each chamber

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.920
will have an easier time
passing proposed legislation

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.163
in their chamber.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.010
This year, if Democrats
were to win the house

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.150
they would be able to decide
which bills come to the floor,

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.710
control committee chairmanships,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.230
add support over a certain investigation

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.530
of Trump's administration.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.543
If Republicans maintain the Senate,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.310
they'll be able to appoint
conservative judges

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.160
and approve Trump's cabinet nominees.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.920
So regardless of where
you lean politically,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.483
get out there and exercise
your right to vote.

00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:50.204
This is the time to make your voice heard.

00:02:03.487 --> 00:02:06.393
Jack, it's burning.
- Yeah I bet.

00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:10.083
- Jack!
- What?

00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.541
(phone going off)

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:12.458
- It hurts!

00:02:13.403 --> 00:02:16.563
This is where I die.
(laughing)

00:02:16.891 --> 00:02:18.056
- [Jack] Aw, look at that, he's in pain,

00:02:18.056 --> 00:02:21.985
he's still making jokes. (laughing)

